{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 2071 PS2 Verified-1 RCA: my new test module lacked the autouse _clean_env fixture its sibling (test_config_ev3a_aliases.py) uses; the CI runner env sets REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM, and env wins over the file, so test_readable_config_resolution_unchanged read True where it asserted the file default False. Reproduced deterministically locally with REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM=1; fixed the CLASS by adding the autouse env-isolation fixture (REBAR_CONFIG/XDG_CONFIG_HOME/REBAR_MCP_*) to the module — green under a hostile env. Amended (Change-Id kept) and pushed PS3. PS2 LLM-Review was +1 with one non-blocking advisory (error_code_for step 4 classifies InsecureUrlError — a deliberate policy rejection subclassing ConfigError — as config_unreadable); deferring that as discovered work rather than expanding this change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787382707118792001,"uuid":"c14ad49b-13ef-4f25-8a2b-8d1c72bfec00"}